%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHahh... Hahh... Phew...\d%K%P
「哈啊、哈啊、呼…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHere's your newspaper, mister!\d%K%P
「大～叔，您的晚报」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dHey, thanks, Mitoko. I've got some barley tea here. Would\nyou like a cup?\d%K%P
「啊，美都子，一直以来多谢你了。\n正好我泡好了麦茶。怎样，要不要来一杯？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, thanks! I was just starting to get thirsty.\d%K%P
「啊～，多谢了。\n那我就恭敬不如从命了～」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dPhew, but it sure grew hot after the end of the rainy\nseason, didn't it? I imagine it must be pretty tough to\nride your bicycle in this weather, especially with all\nthese hills around.\d%K%P
「啊～，说起来梅雨结束后就热起来了。\n最近天气真糟糕啊。是因为这附近斜坡比较多吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dMhm... but it's still a hundred times better than winter\nmornings; on those days, my struggle starts with getting\nout of my warm bed.\d%K%P
「嗯…但是，比起冬天的早晨要强一百多倍。\n那时为了要钻出被子可得做一番斗争的啊」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dAhaha, no kidding. Ah, but you're gonna have exams this\nwinter, aren't you? Shouldn't you start thinking about\nquitting your job for now?\d%K%P
「啊哈哈，说的也是。\n啊，但是你今年冬天也要准备升学考试了吧。\n也差不多该放弃打工了吧？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI'll do it for a little while longer. And I'm gonna have\nmore free time during summer, anyway.\d%K%P
「暂时还会继续的哦。\n暑假还有时间呢」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dBut isn't this summer really important for you? Aren't\nyou going to a summer cram school or something?\d%K%P
「可是，这个夏天就要决定胜负了吧？\n夏季课程的补习班什么的有上吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, there's no chance of that happening. I can't put that\nmuch strain on my guardian.\d%K%P
「啊～，没可能啦。\n『监护人』可能负担不起那种费用吧～」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dNo way. I'm sure your mother wouldn't mind a bit of extra\nstress for her cute daughter. Have you talked to her about\nit yet?\d%K%P
「话是这么说啦，但这毕竟是为了女儿啊。\n即使有点过分问问也是可以的吧？\n和妈妈好好商量过了么？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, um...\d%K%P
「啊，那个…」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dHm? ACtually, now that I think about it, I haven't seen\nyour mo--\d%K%P
「？话说最近，你和你的妈妈…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThank you for the tea! I've gotta hurry and deliver those\nnewspapers now!\d%K%P
「多谢款待！\n那么我要继续送报了！」%K%P
%LCOld Man
%LC大叔
\dO-Okay. Good luck.\d%K%P
「啊、啊啊…加油啊～」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dPhew, that was close. Anyway, only fifteen to go!\d%K%P
「呼，好险好险…\n接下来，还剩１５家～」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHello. I came to visit.\d%K%P
「啊～，您好～」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dAh, I can use you instead of a clock these days, Toko.\nHere you go, today's leftover lunches. I made sure there'd\nbe a lot for you.\d%K%P
「啊，小都子总是在这个时间来啊。\n这个给你，这是今天卖剩下的。\n这次多留了一些」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWow. Thank you! I'll help myself then. ...I'm a bit\nworried about the way you go about running your business,\nbut I'm very grateful!\d%K%P
「哇～，一直以来多谢了。那我就恭敬不如从命了。\n…虽然对你们的经营方针感到疑惑，不过还是多谢了～」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dIt's all right! They cost almost nothing to make anyway!\d%K%P
「没事～没事～。\n反正原价也像垃圾一样便宜」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI've heard about how it works, but I'm not sure if you\nshould say that out loud... Well, whatever. How is he\ndoing?\d%K%P
「虽然知道你的想法，但是在店里说这些话也太…啊，算了。\n那么，怎么样？有努力工作么？」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dAh, he seems to have finally gotten used to the job. I\nstill remember how nervous he was on the first day, haha.\n...But you don't need to ask every day, you know.\d%K%P
「嘿嘿，我已经相当习惯了。\n最开始的时候，总是累得大汗淋漓。\n…啊，你也用不着每天都问同一件事吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dBut you give me the same answer every day too!\d%K%P
「因为大婶你每天的回答都一样啊～」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dAhaha, I guess that's true. Hey, you've got a girl\nwaiting for you here, young man!\d%K%P
「啊哈哈，说的也是。\n喂～，小兄弟，接你的人来了哦～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOh, okay.\d%K%P
「啊，好～的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat are you talking about? I was just passing by on my\nway back from my own job.\d%K%P
「不是啦。\n只是和我送报回去顺道啦」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dAnd you do that every day, always at the precise time his\nshift ends?\d%K%P
「每天都和小兄弟下班的时间一样么？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dMy shift ends at the same time every day.\d%K%P
「每天下班的时间和这个时间一样呢～」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dYesterday, when the guy on evening shift came late and\nyour young man had to stay for an extra hour, I wonder why\na certain girl was lingering outside our shop.\d%K%P
「那前天，\n小兄弟工作时间延长了一个小时，\n你为什么一直在店前等着呢？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHmph, you just can't leave me alone! You don't need to\nworry about things that don't concern you, okay?!\d%K%P
「大婶你真是话多啊～。\n那种事怎么样都好啦」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dWhat's wrong with getting along? What are you acting so\nembarrassed for?\d%K%P
「关系好又不是什么坏事。\n你这孩子害羞什么」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt's because you're trying to make it sound weird. Do you\nget a kick out of teasing people?\d%K%P
「因为大婶说了些莫名其妙的话嘛。\n戏弄人家有意思么？」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dI mean, you're just so obvious I can't help myself.\d%K%P
「因为小都子你太明显啦。\n只是看见就觉得很有意思」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dPfft. I have no idea what you're talking about.\d%K%P
「啊～，我完全不知道您在说什么…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHey, I'm sorry for making you wait, Mitoko.\d%K%P
「抱歉啊美都子，久等了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI said I wasn't waiting, okay?!\d%K%P
「都说了没有在等你！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
%LCBoxed Lunch Lady
%LC便当店的大婶
\dPwh... Hahahahahaha!\d%K%P
「呼…啊哈哈哈哈～」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt's taking more and more time for the sun to set, huh?\d%K%P
「太阳落山，天色已晚了啊～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYeah.\d%K%P
「嗯」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLast week, it would be dark by the time we got home! And\nlast month, it would already be dark when I'd come to pick\nyou up!\d%K%P
「上个星期，回到家时天已经黑了啊。\n还有，上个月，接失业先生的时候也好黑啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWas it? I was so tired from work at the time that I don't\neven remember.\d%K%P
「是那样的吗…\n我那时候回家只觉得非常累，记不住了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou finally got used to the smell of rice, huh. Ahaha.\d%K%P
「看来你终于习惯了啊，米饭的气味。啊哈哈」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's not funny... It was really hard for me at first, you\nknow.\d%K%P
「没那么可笑吧…\n一开始真的很痛苦啊」%K%P
We were walking down the road back home to the Terrace\nHouse Hinosaka.%K%P
我们两人走在通往Terrace House阳之坂的道路上。%K%P
As always, I took the job of pushing her bicycle as she\ntalked about all sorts of things while gesticulating with\nher free hands.%K%P
我推着美都子的自行车，\n而双手已经解放了的美都子一边摆着胳膊，\n一边说着各种各样的话题。%K%P
Not only about what was interesting or fun...%K%P
不仅仅是有意思的、开心的话题。%K%P
But she'd also tell me about the boring parts of her day,\nwhen nothing happened. She lectured me. She talked about\nthe weather. Horoscopes. Anything at all.%K%P
也有无聊的事情，没有什么奇妙历险展开的日子里所发生的一些琐碎，\n以及对我抱怨，还有天气、星座之类的，什么都有。%K%P
Mitoko now walked the same road with me that she used to\nshare with her mother.%K%P
就这样，她和我一起走在，\n她曾经和她的妈妈一同回去的道路上。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dDo you get along with the old ladies there? They're kind\nto anyone who listens to their gossiping. I hope you can\nmanage that much!\d%K%P
「与大婶她们的关系变好了么？\n对于肯陪着自己聊天的人，她们还是很热情的。\n和她们也能好好相处了么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI got used to that, too. I've already received seven\noffers of arranged marriage from them. I told them I was\nin no position to even entertain such an idea, but they\ndon't listen.\d%K%P
「那个也已经习惯了啊。\n来提亲的有７位…\n现在还不想结婚什么的，怎么说都没用」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dPwh! That's right! Mrs. Hashimoto said she had only one\nmore to go before she could call herself the cupid of a\nhundred couples! She's going after everyone right now!\d%K%P
「噗。是啊是啊。\n桥本大婶，她还差一组就撮合成１００对情侣了。\n因此现在她无论是谁的婚事都想掺和一把」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOh god... You know how bad I am at refusing things...\d%K%P
「饶了我吧…\n你也知道我不擅长拒绝别人的要求吧？」%K%P
I started working part-time at the boxed lunch shop near\nthe station from the start of July. On the third day\nfollowing my return home after losing my job.%K%P
我从六月初就开始在车站前的便当店打工。\n这是失去工作返回公寓的第三天的事情。%K%P
Mitoko used to work there, so I got hired on her\nrecommendation alone.%K%P
本来美都子也曾在这店里工作过，\n因此通过她的介绍，我很轻松就被雇佣了。%K%P
I only needed to work from afternoon to evening, so I used\nthe mornings in my quest to find proper employment.%K%P
因为午后开始也没关系，\n因此上午可以腾出时间来找工作。%K%P
Mitoko was happy that I might overcome my fear of rice if\nI had to work with it every day. If possible, though, I\nwould have truly liked to avoid that one part of my new\njob at least.%K%P
而且每天都接触我之前不能吃的米饭，\n因此可能也稍稍克服了偏食的问题。\n虽然我还是不太想吃……%K%P
But then there was one other reason -- perhaps the biggest\none -- why we both liked me working here. Although,\nneither of us could say it out loud.%K%P
还有…\n这是最重要的理由，虽然彼此都没有说出来。%K%P
I could finish my shift pretty much whenever I wanted. As\na result, I could adjust my schedule to be able to go home\nwith Mitoko once her delivery job was finished.%K%P
因为可以在喜欢的时间下班，\n所以可以和打完工的美都子一起回家。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThat's 'cause you told them you were divorced, like a\ntotal fool.\d%K%P
「你还真老老实实说自己是领过证的了啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou know I don't like lying, right?\d%K%P
「你知道我不善于说谎吧？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThey were really excited when you told them, you know.\nThey even came at me with questions. I took pity on you\nand didn't say anything about Ms. Kouno, but you should be\na bit more careful.\d%K%P
「这事说出去的时候，大婶他们也很高兴呢。\n连我都是听说了很多事哦？\n嘛，虽然因为武士的同情也没有告诉老师就是了」%K%P
My colleagues at the new workplace -- all women of\nsubstantial age -- welcomed me with kindness as Mitoko's\nslightly weak-willed uncle.%K%P
在同一个职场的『上了年岁的女性们』，\n非常亲切地把我以『小都子靠不住的叔父』的身份，\n请到了自己家里。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
Ms. Honoka married the owner of a cafe in the next town\nover, and went for a three month trip around the world for\nher honeymoon.%K%P
穗香小姐与附近城市某咖啡店的老板再婚，\n现在正在进行着为期三个月的环球新婚旅行。\n※译注：NETA《女仆咖啡巧克拉》的结城大介父亲再婚的新婚旅行。%K%P
They invited Mitoko along, but not wanting to get between\nthe two, she refused and stayed behind.%K%P
虽然也邀请了美都子一起去旅行，\n但她一心希望母亲幸福因而拒绝了。%K%P
And to look after her during that time, they called an\nuncle that Mitoko got along with very well -- Ms. Honoka's\n\dyounger brother.\d In other words, me.%K%P
在此期间，为照顾孤身一人的美都子，\n穗香小姐的弟弟、同时也是美都子很喜欢的叔父——我，\n被叫到这里来了。%K%P
...We figured it'd be easier to keep the truth hidden\ncompared to the school, so we added that bit about blood\nrelations.%K%P
…为了减少这个谎言在学校暴露的风险，\n她也给我准备了血缘关系这一措施。%K%P
As such, the Yoshimura Honoka I dreamt about descended\nupon this reality in a slightly different form than I had\nexpected -- as her fabricated maiden name.%K%P
于是，我所梦寐以求的『芳村穗香』，\n光荣地成为了穗香小姐虚假的旧名。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBesides, trying to hide my marriage information has\nalready gotten me in trouble in the past.\d%K%P
「还有啊，\n之前，我把{离婚史:这件事}瞒着，结果倒了大霉啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Really?\d%K%P
「…是么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dDon't you think my face has filled out a little over the\npast few months?\d%K%P
「你不觉得这几个月我的脸都肿起来了吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, I guess you do look a bit more like a somewhat\ntrustworthy man now. You used to be so lean I was afraid\nthe wind might break you in half.\d%K%P
「嗯，已经是一个相当坚强的男人脸了～。\n以前看起来十分消瘦，简直就是一个瘦弱的小孩」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHey.\d%K%P
「喂」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAhahaha... I'm just kidding! But you really do look\nbetter, especially since you no longer look as gloomy as\nbefore!\d%K%P
「啊哈哈哈…开个玩笑啦。\n但是，现在确实好多了。\n最起码已经不让人感到厌烦了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry...\d%K%P
「抱歉…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHow many times do I have to say that's not the right time\nto apologize?\d%K%P
「所以说，这里用不着道歉吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's right. Ahaha.\d%K%P
「说的是呢，啊哈哈」%K%P
I couldn't admit it was mostly thanks to her. She'd be\nlaughing at me until the end of the day.%K%P
虽然『这也是多亏了你哦』之类的话，\n因为笑着而没有说出口。%K%P
But it was true that I felt grateful to her from the\nbottom of my heart.%K%P
但我确实是打心底里感谢美都子。%K%P
I could do my best because she was there for me. She was\nmy greatest benefactor, presenting me with a goal to\nstrive for -- something I thought I'd lost a year ago.%K%P
正是在最需要遇到她的时候遇到了她，\n我才会继续努力下去，直到现在。\n她重新给了我已然失去好几年的生活目标，她，是我的恩人。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI dunno, the pace of the conversation always goes all\nover the place when I talk to you. You should react to my\njokes more quickly and efficiently, if you know what I\nmean.\d%K%P
「是啊，和失业先生聊天的话，\n不管什么话题都会跑偏。\n以后，你得说得更直接一些啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYeah, I'll try.\d%K%P
「嗯，我会努力的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dGeez. That's exactly what I'm talking about!\d%K%P
「都说了不应该是这种反应吧～」%K%P
And so, just as the sun had completely set, we found\nourselves at the steps of our good old Terrace House\nHinosaka.%K%P
聊着各种各样的话题，天也差不多黑了下来。\n今天也是好容易才到家…到达Terrace House阳之坂。%K%P
I wondered if we'd be able to make it home before\nnightfall tomorrow.%K%P
明天，能在天还没黑之前到家么？%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI'm home.\d%K%P
「我回来了～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWe're home.\d%K%P
「我回来了」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAh, welcome back. Dinner's ready.\d%K%P
「啊，欢迎～。\n已经做好饭了哦」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dA-Aha... Ahaha...\d%K%P
「啊、啊哈、啊哈哈…」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWell then, let's dig in!\d%K%P
「那么，我要开动～了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dL-Let's dig in...\d%K%P
「我、我开动了…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAha... Ahah... Ahahahaha...\d%K%P
「啊哈、啊哈、啊哈哈哈哈」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat's so funny?\d%K%P
「刚刚有什么奇怪的么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I'm sorry!\d%K%P
「十、十分抱歉！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHmph!\d%K%P
「哼」%K%P
It seemed like apologizing here was the right choice.%K%P
看来刚才的道歉是完全正确的啊。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dNow, now, Ms. Landlord. You aren't a child anymore, so\ncalm down. I'm sure you're just upset because you're\nhungry, aren't you? Come now, eat up so you'll grow big\nand strong.\d%K%P
「喂，房东小姐。你不是小孩了，所以是不会生气的吧。\n一定是因为饿了才感到不爽吧？\n来，多吃点才会长大哦？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...!!\d%K%P
「～～～唔！！！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dM-Ms. Kaya... Stop... Please, just stop.\d%K%P
「夏、夏夜小姐…请作罢，请务必作罢」%K%P
Mitoko's straight-laced disposition clearly wasn't able to\nhandle the kind of multilayered sarcasm this woman\nspecialized in doling out.%K%P
这个人计划好了那接二连三的冷嘲热讽，\n实施起来后对像美都子这样坦率的人十分有效。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dHere, open wiiide.\d%K%P
「来，张～嘴？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI can eat by myself!!!\d%K%P
「我开动了！！！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHahh...\d%K%P
「哈啊…」%K%P
Amagi Kaya -- the tenant of the Terrace House Hinosaka's\nRoom #5.%K%P
－－－天城夏夜。\nTerrace House阳之坂『５号房』的住户。%K%P
And -- somehow -- my new neighbor.%K%P
在我总算注意到的时候，已经变成了我的邻居。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAh, Osamu! This is real damn good! I mean, you normally\nwouldn't praise your own cooking like that, but I think it\nturned out really well.\d%K%P
「啊，理君。这个很好吃的哦。\n虽然不该由我来说，不过感觉真的不错～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIs it lamb?\d%K%P
「是羊羔肉么？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dYeah, grilled lamb. Try it.\d%K%P
「嗯，香草烧的。\n尝尝么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, okay. ...Um, I can eat by myself.\d%K%P
「啊，好的………我自己会吃的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d......\d%K%P
「………（嚼嚼）」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWhy're you acting so shy? I mean, we used to live\ntogether.\d%K%P
「不用客气啦。\n我们都是同居过的关系了～」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...It's nothing.\d%K%P
「唔………没什么」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dNo one asked you what's wrong, though.\d%K%P
「『怎么了理？突然绷紧了脸』什么的，\n没人这么说哦？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...!!\d%K%P
「～唔」%K%P
This situation was developing in line with Ms. Kaya's\ncalculations, no doubt. She was a far better strategist\nthan the two of us.%K%P
变成这种状况，\n是夏夜小姐都计算好的呢，\n还是两人战略水平不同呢。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
There was no way our extra principled landlord would have\nlet Ms. Kaya stay in my room, let alone anyone else's,\nwhen she suddenly came over with that huge truck full of\nluggage.%K%P
突然将搬家的卡车停了过来，\n在我和其他住户的房间留宿什么的，\n这对家里爱唠叨的风纪房东小姐来说怎么可能认同？但是…%K%P
But -- at the same time -- she found herself unable to\nforce a lone woman out onto the streets with nowhere to\ngo.%K%P
夏夜小姐从她原本的公寓搬出来后，也不去另找其它住处。\n虽然天也不冷，但是对他人很仁慈的房东小姐也不可能让她流露街头。%K%P
Meanwhile, the Terrace House Hinosaka had five rooms in\ntotal. So what, then, was the most natural course of\naction?%K%P
而且Terrace House阳之坂，实际上总共有５间房。\n因此能得出的结论是…？%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHey, Mr. Laid-off. Don't you dare leave that rice.\d%K%P
「等下，失业先生。\n不好好吃饭可不行哦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, okay...\d%K%P
「啊，好的…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWhy force him to eat something he doesn't want? I think\nhe can eat whatever he wants as long as we make sure he\ngets all his vitamins.\d%K%P
「他不想吃也不用非让他吃啊？\n反正营养不缺不就好了吧？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dNo way. I was this close to curing him of his affliction.\nI'm not giving up now.\d%K%P
「不行的。\n好不容易治好的偏食不坚持下去可不行啊」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dHe's already getting enough carbs through bread and\npasta, though. I think he should just relax and eat what\nhe likes.\d%K%P
「我可是做好了面包和意大利面的主食呢。\n我觉得享受美味的食物才是最重要的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dDid your parents never teach you to clean your plate?\d%K%P
「『不要挑食，什么都要吃』，\n你小时候没有被这么教育过么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I am thoroughly ashamed of myself.\d%K%P
「………真的是非常抱歉」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
After Ms. Kaya moved in and took all her cutting-edge\ncooking equipment into her room, it took about ten seconds\nfor her to end up flipping the house's circuit breakers.%K%P
之后，夏夜小姐把电磁炉拿进屋里开始做料理，\n１０秒后公寓跳闸了。%K%P
Her excuse for doing this was, direct quote, \dI just\nwanted to cook for you, Osamu.\d I swear I felt a fuse\nblowing when she said that, and it certainly wasn't in the\nhouse...%K%P
但是，那时她说的『想给理做饭』，\n做的应该是其它什么能引起跳闸的内容…%K%P
At any rate, before I knew it, she'd been awarded the\nprivilege of using the gas stove in the landlord's room,\nalong with the key to said room.%K%P
被发现跳闸之后，夏夜小姐便趁机得到了房东小姐房间的钥匙，\n以及那里煤气炉的使用权。%K%P
And ever since then, about twice a week, Ms. Kaya would\ncook dinner for me and Mitoko.%K%P
那之后，每周两次，夏夜小姐就在这个房间，\n为我和美都子做料理。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dBesides, bread probably goes better with what I cooked\ntoday.\d%K%P
「而且，本来今天的料理和面包一起吃也很合适吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWe got fried shrimp from the shop today, so make it rice,\nokay?\d%K%P
「今天吃的是天麸罗吧。\n因此也要吃点饭啊」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dUgh, I can smell the fat from here. That doesn't look\nhealthy at all to me, rice or no rice.\d%K%P
「哇，好腻。\n这个要是和饭搭配的话对身体可不会很好的哦」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dMr. Laid-off was the one who fried those! Are you just\ngonna let what you made yourself go to waste, huh?!\d%K
「是失业先生在烹饪吧？\n自己做的东西能随便么！」%K
Have bread
吃面包
Have rice
请盛点饭
